    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 83.29. Facing Montero, he benefits from a favorable platoon advantage (+14%) and the premium hitting environment, positioning him as the primary engine for power and run production. Joining him in the elite tier is **Luis Robert Jr.** (75.93), whose matchup against the lefty P\u00e9rez is a prime target for high-ceiling performance. We are also capitalizing on a significant SP vulnerability as **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) squares off against the declining arm of Scherzer. The +19% SP skill adjustment and a strong #2 spot in the order make him an essential play, particularly given the league\u2019s acute need for reliable output.\n\nWhile the core is set, the decision to bench **Miguel Vargas** (51.45) was a close call. He posted a strong xwOBA of 0.390, but ultimately, the opportunity cost in our constrained lineup was too high; his efficiency profile could not surpass the situational leverage provided by **Curtis Mead** or **Jacob Wilson**, whose roles at the top of their respective lineups offer more guaranteed volume for our counting categories. We are also closely monitoring **Nasim Nunez**; despite his #9 spot, his +4% \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus against Scherzer makes him a sneaky stolen base threat\u2014a vital factor for our scarcity-driven strategy. \n\nCaution is warranted for **Drake Baldwin** and **Luis Robert Jr.**, as both currently carry a 31% rain risk, which could disrupt their availability or curtail their game-time impact. Furthermore, while we like the matchup for **Heliot Ramos** (59.55), he faces a slight degradation in score due to the \"Elite Hold\" status of Sproat, which dampens his stolen base potential despite the favorable wind conditions. We will continue to monitor the weather patterns for the **Drake Baldwin** start, but given the current projection, the lineup remains the most efficient configuration to maximize our 5x5 standing.",
